== DEVIATIONS from PLAN.txt
- Global "pattern explains x" tests (C lengths, streaks) use the upper tail of the between-pattern sum of squares (a variance statistic: only large values mean the pattern explains x), not "two-sided around the null mean" as the plan's general wording for group-mean tests says. Per-pattern tests are two-sided as planned.
- Added (descriptive, not in any family): the share-up and x differences in A2 with their own p, the signed-streak trend IC, vol60 vs |y| context ICs, |y| by fifth tables, in H a luck p against random picks of the same size in each quarter (5,000 shuffles), and in F an after-the-fact split of the lag-1 result by period (qn 1-7, 8-21, 14-21), chosen after seeing the quarter table: descriptive only, no p value.
- Seeds: C length 4 uses 20261104 + 4 = 20261108, the same seed as the streak test, exactly as pre-registered.
